---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import ArchitectureDiagram from "../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Architecture"
  description="A conceptual AeglysAI authorization architecture distinguishing implemented baselines and offline non-enforcing research from future production control integration."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="02 / Architecture"
    title="Explicit policy. Informed decisions."
    description="A conceptual view of the authorization path and the research extensions that could connect evidence, bounded decisions and continuous feedback."
  />
  <div class="container page-content">
    <ArchitectureDiagram detailed />
    <aside class="notice"><h2>Research completion does not grant enforcement</h2><p>Model D research implementation is complete for its bounded offline experimental scope. The diagram separates the implemented baseline path, completed offline research and planned operational extensions. It is not an implemented adaptive enforcement path. <code>enforcement_authority=NONE</code>; external validation, drift and mock-feedback limitations remain.</p></aside>
    <section
      class="section capability-list"
      aria-label="Architecture capabilities"
    >
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Deterministic Policy</h2>
          <p>
            Role-based authorization and attribute conditions provide explicit
            rules in the implemented baselines. They form the foundation for
            investigating policy-bounded adaptation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Implemented" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Contextual Risk</h2>
          <p>
            Model C uses deterministic contextual risk. This rule-based
            capability is distinct from learned behavioral anomaly detection.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Implemented" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Behavioral Intelligence</h2>
          <p>
            Completed offline experimental behavioral inference and bounded eligibility/drift diagnostics produce evidence, not access decisions. Internal synthetic checks do not establish external effectiveness or mature drift monitoring.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Research Implementation Complete" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Experimental Recommendation Integration</h2>
          <p>
            Completed offline research integration produces non-enforcing recommendations. Model D has enforcement_authority=NONE; production adaptive decisions remain a planned extension.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Research Implementation Complete" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">05</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Mock Feedback and Future Live Feedback</h2>
          <p>
            In-memory mock-feedback simulation is implemented for offline research; response effectiveness remains unestablished. Live telemetry and continuous production feedback are planned extensions, with stability and operational costs unresolved.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Planned Research" />
      </article>
    </section>
    <aside class="notice">
      <h2>A map of the investigation</h2>
      <p>
        The diagram distinguishes existing baseline capabilities, completed offline experimental research and proposed operational extensions. It does not specify deployed services, live telemetry coverage or an implemented production adaptive decision engine.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
